# Frontend Conventions

Dashboard lives in `web/static/` (source) and `internal/server/static/`
(embedded). After editing web/static/, sync:
```bash
cp web/static/*.html internal/server/static/
```
Then rebuild the Go binary to pick up changes.

## Stack

- **xterm.js** (CDN) - full terminal emulation, handles all ANSI/colors/cursor
- **Vanilla JS** - no framework, no build step
- No HTMX, no Tailwind, no Chart.js (removed - xterm.js handles rendering)

## Pages

- `index.html` - run list dashboard. Polls `/api/runs` every 2s.
- `session.html` - terminal viewer. WebSocket to `/ws/:name`.

## Status Colors (Consistent Everywhere)

- **Green** = streaming (command actively producing output, >50 bytes/sec)
- **Yellow** = awaiting (session active but idle >1s, waiting for input)
- **Red** = ended (session closed, command finished or killed)

## xterm.js Setup

```js
const term = new Terminal({
  disableStdin: true,   // read-only viewer
  convertEol: true,     // handle \n without \r
  scrollback: 50000,
});
```

Loaded from CDN (jsdelivr). Addons: fit (responsive), web-links (clickable URLs).

## WebSocket Protocol

- Binary messages: raw terminal bytes → `term.write(data)`
- Text messages: JSON status updates → `{"status":"ended"}`
- Burst detection: track bytes/sec in 1-second windows to distinguish
  real output (streaming) from keystroke echoes (awaiting)

## Encryption (Tier 2, Not Built Yet)

Browser will decrypt with WebCrypto API using key from URL fragment
(`#key=base64...`). Fragment never sent to server. Decrypt each chunk
before writing to xterm.js. No JS crypto libraries.
